; v_rel = v_observer - v_observed.
; two-participant mantra: both inputs are "velocity" from different entities.
; the proof graph supplies both participants' values via scope-entity dispatch.
; uses math-op path (subtraction) in execute-mantra, not krama/kriya.
; shabda has math-op:subtraction — handles forward and inverse.
;
; multi-entity: derive-step must not fire this blindly with one velocity.
; match-mantra routes it through relative-vps which collects both values.

(mantra relative-velocity-mantra
  (vishesa linear-motion-varga)
  (varga physics-mantra)
  (swarupa relative-velocity)
  (phala relative-velocity)
  (yukta multi-entity)
  (janya velocity velocity))
